OMP_NUM_THREADS environment is not set. Defaulting to 1 thread. (src/comm.cpp:98)
  using 1 OpenMP thread(s) per MPI task
package omp 2
set 2 OpenMP thread(s) per MPI task
using multi-threaded neighbor list subroutines
# Hydrogenation-assisted graphene origami (HAGO), AIREBO, 300 K self-folding
# Run:  lmp -in in.origami  [-var T 300 -var nsteps 200000 -var data origami.data]

variable    T       index 300
variable    nsteps  index 200000          # 0.5 fs steps -> 100 ps
variable    data    index origami.data
variable    seed    index 4928

units       metal
atom_style  atomic
boundary    s s s                          # free sheet in vacuum
read_data   ${data}
read_data   origami.data
Reading data file ...
  orthogonal box = (-60 -60 -60) to (139.52 98.1224 60)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
  reading atoms ...
  1248 atoms
  read_data CPU = 0.003 seconds

# AIREBO: REBO + LJ (vdW, needed for layers sticking) + torsion
pair_style  airebo 3.0 1 1
pair_coeff  * * CH.airebo C H
Reading airebo potential file CH.airebo with DATE: 2011-10-25

neighbor    2.0 bin
neigh_modify delay 0 every 1 check yes

group       C type 1
1216 atoms in group C
group       H type 2
32 atoms in group H

# energy components: c_eA[1]=REBO, [2]=LJ (vdW adhesion), [3]=torsion
compute     eA all pair airebo
compute     rg C gyration
compute     peat all pe/atom

thermo_style custom step time temp pe c_eA[1] c_eA[2] c_eA[3] c_rg
thermo      1000
thermo_modify norm no

# ---- 1. relax the as-built sheet (H strips buckle here) ----
min_style   cg
minimize    1e-8 1e-6 3000 30000
